title: "The AI Production Function: Code Capital, Context Capital, and Computational Labor"
abstract: >-
  A generalized production framework for AI-native economies: a conceptual
  re-grounding and a falsifiable research program, not yet an empirically
  validated theory. It re-grounds the classical factors as Code Capital,
  Context Capital, and Computational Work, derives Y = A * C^alpha * X^beta *
  W^gamma, proves it nests the Cobb-Douglas function, specifies how each factor
  can be operationalized, confronts the simultaneity problem in identifying the
  elasticities, weighs the labor interpretation of compute against
  capital-service and intermediate-input alternatives, and states falsifiable
  hypotheses.
